WEBVTT

00:00:02.680 --> 00:00:06.390
Ya know, I just wanna find something
only I can do!

00:00:06.470 --> 00:00:08.560
-Totally.
-You're going to art school, right?

00:00:08.640 --> 00:00:12.310
It's nice knowing what you wanna do.
Hopefully I'll figure it out in 4 years,

00:00:12.390 --> 00:00:13.940
but I have no idea now.

00:00:14.020 --> 00:00:14.940
Don't worry!

00:00:15.020 --> 00:00:16.940
You'll have a goal no matter where you go.

00:00:17.020 --> 00:00:19.070
Just do what your gut tells you, ya know?

00:00:19.150 --> 00:00:20.530
Totally!

00:00:20.780 --> 00:00:22.900
<i>Something only you can do...</i>

00:00:24.280 --> 00:00:27.490
<i>What's something that only I can do?</i>

00:00:43.300 --> 00:00:47.760
AIR SELF-DEFENSE FORCE

00:00:55.730 --> 00:00:57.810
Keep coming.

00:01:12.330 --> 00:01:13.160
Okay. Open it.

00:01:21.130 --> 00:01:22.630
Mambo Viking 11.

00:01:23.170 --> 00:01:24.590
<i>After airborne.</i>

00:01:24.670 --> 00:01:27.380
<i>Maintain 2000 for area keep.</i>

00:01:27.970 --> 00:01:31.140
<i>Wind 080 at five.</i>

00:01:31.510 --> 00:01:34.310
<i>Runway 28 cleared for takeoff.</i>

00:01:34.770 --> 00:01:36.190
<i>Cleared for takeoff.</i>

00:01:36.560 --> 00:01:38.100
Mambo Viking 11.

00:01:53.620 --> 00:01:54.830
Amakasu.

00:01:55.580 --> 00:01:57.120
Amakasu!

00:01:58.000 --> 00:01:58.830
Yes, ma'am?

00:01:59.080 --> 00:02:03.380
Take this external interview application
to Flight Leader Kakiyasu.

00:02:03.880 --> 00:02:05.420
She's in Hangar 8.

00:02:06.010 --> 00:02:08.300
Hangar 8?

00:02:08.590 --> 00:02:10.390
But I've never gone to the northern...

00:02:10.680 --> 00:02:12.220
I'll lend you my moped.

00:02:12.300 --> 00:02:13.430
You'll be fine.

00:02:13.510 --> 00:02:15.060
-Ms. Akishima.
-Yes, sir!

00:02:15.560 --> 00:02:20.060
-Ogawa from the Tsuchiya Publishing...
-How is lending me your moped a solution?

00:02:20.150 --> 00:02:24.320
I've never been to the air test wing
or even knew that this Kakiyasu existed.

00:02:26.780 --> 00:02:28.200
Huh? Did you say something?

00:02:30.700 --> 00:02:31.530
Here.

00:02:31.990 --> 00:02:34.370
Thanks for taking care of it.

00:02:37.580 --> 00:02:39.870
I never expected it would be Amakasu.

00:02:40.120 --> 00:02:43.290
It seems she did very well
on the aptitude test.

00:02:43.790 --> 00:02:46.670
We'll just have to wait
and see what happens.

00:02:47.460 --> 00:02:49.590
-Oh, my tea leaf.
-Is it standing for good luck?

00:02:50.260 --> 00:02:51.340
It's broken...

00:02:53.050 --> 00:02:55.600
It only goes up to Hangar 7.

00:02:56.310 --> 00:02:58.930
Um... Hangar 8... Hangar 8...

00:02:59.020 --> 00:03:00.060
Yakult.

00:03:00.140 --> 00:03:01.810
Yakult... Ya--

00:03:03.770 --> 00:03:05.770
Don't you like Yakult?

00:03:05.980 --> 00:03:07.030
Here you go.

00:03:07.190 --> 00:03:08.740
STRAWBERRY YAKULT JOA

00:03:10.110 --> 00:03:11.110
Most likely,

00:03:12.030 --> 00:03:14.620
the place you're looking for

00:03:14.740 --> 00:03:16.620
is over there.

00:03:18.580 --> 00:03:20.250
Thank you very much.

00:03:27.710 --> 00:03:29.050
HANGAR 8

00:03:31.300 --> 00:03:34.550
Um... excuse me...

00:03:36.430 --> 00:03:40.810
Is there a flight leader
named Kakiyasu here...?

00:03:43.520 --> 00:03:45.190
Could this be

00:03:45.270 --> 00:03:50.070
systemic bullying concocted by women who
can't get married and other old weirdos?

00:03:51.570 --> 00:03:52.400
A pool?

00:03:55.660 --> 00:03:57.580
At a time like this...

00:04:04.040 --> 00:04:05.670
Ah, Goro!

00:04:05.750 --> 00:04:08.380
The world is such a cold, cruel place.

00:04:08.500 --> 00:04:12.630
Let me go back to the warmth
of your fluffy tummy.

00:04:24.400 --> 00:04:31.360
DRAGON PILOT: HISONE &amp; MASOTAN

00:04:41.250 --> 00:04:43.500
Since long ago, we have been searching

00:04:43.580 --> 00:04:46.960
for the means to coexist
with Organic Transformed Flyers.

00:04:47.380 --> 00:04:51.210
Possession of Organic Transformed Flyers
allowed the nation to flourish,

00:04:51.420 --> 00:04:54.590
but also created a target for
neighboring countries to attack.

00:04:55.130 --> 00:04:59.970
As a result, our ancestors camouflaged
and hid the Organic Transformed Flyers

00:05:00.560 --> 00:05:03.230
with kites, feathered kimonos,
and banners.

00:05:03.730 --> 00:05:07.940
When control over them passed from
the shogunate to the government,

00:05:08.150 --> 00:05:12.530
concealment duties were run by
the Imperial Army and Naval air forces.

00:05:12.610 --> 00:05:15.740
Post-WWII, those duties were passed
to us, the Air Self-Defense Force.

00:05:16.070 --> 00:05:17.990
And what you encountered

00:05:18.070 --> 00:05:20.280
was one of those
Organic Transformed Flyers.

00:05:20.370 --> 00:05:23.750
A dragon, Hisone Amakasu.

00:05:27.330 --> 00:05:30.040
She wasn't listening, was she,
Ms. Kakiyasu?

00:05:30.210 --> 00:05:32.590
Commander Sosoda, it's only natural.

00:05:32.670 --> 00:05:35.130
Consider that she just met
a fantastical creature,

00:05:35.720 --> 00:05:40.300
was suddenly swallowed by said creature,
and just as suddenly spewed out.

00:05:45.100 --> 00:05:46.770
It's no use. He won't spit her up.

00:05:46.850 --> 00:05:48.270
Add in the emetic drugs!

00:05:54.110 --> 00:05:55.110
Vomit...

00:05:55.360 --> 00:05:56.400
Wonderful!

00:05:57.150 --> 00:05:59.570
Rather than fearing the creature itself,

00:05:59.660 --> 00:06:02.120
you seem more concerned
with being vomited out.

00:06:02.240 --> 00:06:06.330
You cope well with abnormal situations
and have flexible judgment.

00:06:06.960 --> 00:06:08.290
Hisone Amakasu,

00:06:08.370 --> 00:06:11.670
starting today, you'll join
the Organic Transformed Flyers,

00:06:11.840 --> 00:06:16.840
OTF for short, and become a dragon pilot.

00:06:16.920 --> 00:06:17.930
D...

00:06:18.590 --> 00:06:19.760
Dragon Pilot?!

00:06:19.840 --> 00:06:22.350
IT IS INSANE

00:06:22.850 --> 00:06:27.140
First off, let's officially
introduce you to the OTF.

00:06:27.520 --> 00:06:30.400
Um, I... I can't...

00:06:41.910 --> 00:06:45.290
The OTF are ordinarily deployed
from here, Hangar 8.

00:06:45.990 --> 00:06:47.290
Airman Okonogi.

00:06:47.700 --> 00:06:48.790
Y-Yes.

00:06:49.250 --> 00:06:51.420
He is the OTF maintenance leader.

00:06:52.460 --> 00:06:55.000
I'm pleased to make your acquaintance.

00:06:57.170 --> 00:06:59.010
You're very impressive, if I may say.

00:06:59.630 --> 00:07:01.640
To be chosen by an OTF.

00:07:01.890 --> 00:07:03.180
Chosen?

00:07:03.470 --> 00:07:07.100
To disperse their intense metabolic heat,

00:07:07.180 --> 00:07:09.140
the OTF need to fly in the sky.

00:07:09.690 --> 00:07:14.610
But for the past three years, this OTF
hasn't accepted any Dragon Pilots.

00:07:15.230 --> 00:07:20.110
Without a pilot, it can't fly much less
navigate an emergency situation.

00:07:20.860 --> 00:07:24.700
We've been able to cool it with the pool,
but we're at our limit.

00:07:24.950 --> 00:07:28.290
And you are our savior.

00:07:29.370 --> 00:07:30.290
N-No...

00:07:30.370 --> 00:07:32.790
I couldn't be a savior...

00:07:33.080 --> 00:07:35.090
Raising the OTF on the lift.

00:08:08.410 --> 00:08:11.830
-He's actually behaving today.
-Usually, he's like a spoiled brat.

00:08:12.120 --> 00:08:13.830
Now, try touching him!

00:08:13.920 --> 00:08:15.250
It's a strange encounter,

00:08:15.330 --> 00:08:16.840
just like E.T.!

00:08:17.590 --> 00:08:18.420
You don't know it?

00:08:18.800 --> 00:08:20.170
Look, just like this,

00:08:20.260 --> 00:08:21.670
take your finger and touch it!

00:08:24.220 --> 00:08:25.680
I...I can't...

00:08:34.310 --> 00:08:35.940
The OTF made the first move.

00:08:36.020 --> 00:08:37.020
She's the real deal.

00:08:37.440 --> 00:08:39.690
That's incredible, Amakasu!

00:08:43.030 --> 00:08:43.990
Amakasu?!

00:08:44.070 --> 00:08:46.950
Emetic! Get the emetic!

00:08:49.490 --> 00:08:51.450
AIR DEVELOPMENT &amp; TEST WING
WOMEN'S BARRACKS

00:08:51.790 --> 00:08:55.540
Amakasu, you'll be residing
in these barracks from today.

00:08:55.960 --> 00:08:58.750
-I can't... I can't...
-OTF requires concealment,

00:08:58.840 --> 00:09:01.090
-so don't discuss it with others...
-That's why...

00:09:01.170 --> 00:09:02.380
I said I can't...

00:09:18.810 --> 00:09:21.020
Um... Would you like this?

00:09:30.200 --> 00:09:33.790
Cool it in the fridge!
It's freaking lukewarm!

00:09:34.330 --> 00:09:36.290
This is Airman 2nd Class Nao Kaizaki.

00:09:36.460 --> 00:09:39.500
She's also a Dragon Pilot cadet.
Get close with her.

00:09:40.000 --> 00:09:42.130
We aren't going to get along.

00:09:42.420 --> 00:09:44.090
I'll bully the hell out of you.

00:09:50.050 --> 00:09:52.430
<i>When being ejected from the OTF,</i>

00:09:53.220 --> 00:09:56.520
<i>cross both arms to reduce friction</i>

00:09:56.810 --> 00:09:59.270
<i>and protect your esophagus from harm.</i>

00:10:00.650 --> 00:10:01.520
<i>In an emergency...</i>

00:10:01.610 --> 00:10:04.610
Will I be thrown up again?

00:10:04.780 --> 00:10:07.950
By the way, you won't go out
the front door in an emergency.

00:10:09.360 --> 00:10:14.240
To prevent that, be sure to learn
the regular ejection procedure well.

00:10:15.830 --> 00:10:16.910
I can't...

00:10:17.000 --> 00:10:19.040
Amakasu's losing her spine!

00:10:19.120 --> 00:10:20.250
Hey, hey, hey!

00:10:20.630 --> 00:10:22.090
Keep coming!

00:10:37.060 --> 00:10:38.190
This is...

00:10:38.560 --> 00:10:39.390
We told you.

00:10:39.730 --> 00:10:41.480
-Keep coming!
-Since long ago,

00:10:41.610 --> 00:10:44.150
humans have had to camouflage the dragons.

00:10:44.730 --> 00:10:47.940
Since that is the duty
of the Air Self-Defense Force...

00:10:48.360 --> 00:10:51.280
What else could it be
other than a plane? Idiot.

00:10:52.240 --> 00:10:53.330
Rather than camouflage,

00:10:54.080 --> 00:10:55.490
it feels more like cosplay.

00:10:58.080 --> 00:11:00.080
Airman 3rd Class Amakasu,

00:11:00.210 --> 00:11:02.040
prepare for embarkation immediately.

00:11:02.130 --> 00:11:03.130
Huh?

00:11:03.250 --> 00:11:05.170
Before your flight training,

00:11:05.250 --> 00:11:08.590
you need to practice camouflaging the OTF
as a fighter aircraft.

00:11:08.970 --> 00:11:11.300
The OTF is set up and ready to go.

00:11:11.590 --> 00:11:13.390
Now, go get closer.

00:11:16.560 --> 00:11:17.560
You'll be fine.

00:11:17.810 --> 00:11:20.060
Just do exactly as directed
in the training video.

00:11:20.480 --> 00:11:23.230
You were chosen by the OTF.

00:11:39.710 --> 00:11:41.000
What are you waiting for?

00:11:41.290 --> 00:11:42.830
Secure your headpiece

00:11:42.920 --> 00:11:45.090
and let the OTF swallow you up.

00:11:48.340 --> 00:11:49.460
I...

00:11:52.090 --> 00:11:53.140
I...

00:11:54.430 --> 00:11:56.430
can't do it!

00:11:57.680 --> 00:11:58.520
Huh?

00:11:58.600 --> 00:11:59.520
What?

00:12:05.360 --> 00:12:09.190
You moron! You came this far
just to chicken out?!

00:12:09.280 --> 00:12:11.650
-She's screwing with us!
-What's the meaning of this?

00:12:12.860 --> 00:12:16.580
If you wanted to back out,
you had plenty of opportunities to do so.

00:12:16.990 --> 00:12:17.910
Why now?

00:12:17.990 --> 00:12:19.200
Fifteen times!

00:12:19.700 --> 00:12:21.580
I tried to back out 15 times.

00:12:21.660 --> 00:12:24.460
I said I can't. I especially can't.

00:12:24.920 --> 00:12:28.210
But every time you just ignored me!

00:12:28.550 --> 00:12:31.010
-Ah... Amakasu...
-Besides, my term is set!

00:12:31.380 --> 00:12:35.760
I was reassigned without being consulted,
and my term was extended, too!

00:12:35.840 --> 00:12:39.510
Is that not in violation
of the Labor Standards Act?!

00:12:39.600 --> 00:12:45.060
If I were to get on Twitter about this,
you'd have a huge problem on your hands!

00:12:45.150 --> 00:12:48.110
I don't even have a Twitter!

00:12:48.190 --> 00:12:49.730
-You...
-I can't believe it!

00:12:49.860 --> 00:12:52.690
Dragons, being puked out
the front, or the back...

00:12:52.780 --> 00:12:55.160
being pushed around
by some elementary school jerk...

00:12:55.240 --> 00:12:56.070
Why you little--

00:12:56.160 --> 00:12:57.530
You don't get to be indignant!

00:12:57.990 --> 00:13:02.080
Did you forget Self-Defense Forces Law,
Article 58 about behaving with dignity?

00:13:02.160 --> 00:13:05.580
Your hair may barely meet the standards,
but it's hardly appropriate here!

00:13:05.670 --> 00:13:08.460
I gave you my Joa
because I mistook you to be a kid!

00:13:08.540 --> 00:13:10.340
Actually, I feel I've been duped!

00:13:10.420 --> 00:13:13.420
I, too, have my own circumstances
and thoughts!

00:13:14.050 --> 00:13:16.760
I... I think...

00:13:19.300 --> 00:13:24.060
orange Joa tastes better than strawberry!

00:13:26.350 --> 00:13:27.190
Joa?

00:13:29.820 --> 00:13:34.280
Hiso Maso!

00:13:37.110 --> 00:13:39.030
Amakasu!

00:13:39.990 --> 00:13:42.620
I'm sorry it's so sudden.

00:13:42.910 --> 00:13:47.870
Yeah, it was really abrupt.
I'd be worried about me, too.

00:13:48.420 --> 00:13:52.250
At this rate, my future is going to be
controlled by utter darkness...

00:13:53.710 --> 00:13:55.010
I'll call you later!

00:13:57.050 --> 00:13:59.430
She's chattier than I thought.

00:13:59.550 --> 00:14:00.640
Amakasu.

00:14:01.300 --> 00:14:03.010
-I'm a chatterbox.
-Huh?

00:14:04.060 --> 00:14:05.140
Rather,

00:14:06.140 --> 00:14:11.020
I've got a huge personality problem!

00:14:13.900 --> 00:14:14.730
I tend to...

00:14:14.860 --> 00:14:17.240
always say what I think.

00:14:18.070 --> 00:14:22.280
My parents said that I should always
express my thoughts.

00:14:22.370 --> 00:14:24.040
I think it's a good thing.

00:14:24.120 --> 00:14:28.290
Like, if a fat person told me
they're worried about getting fat,

00:14:28.370 --> 00:14:31.170
I'd immediately tell them,
"Yes, you certainly are fat."

00:14:31.540 --> 00:14:32.540
I see.

00:14:32.710 --> 00:14:35.460
Even when you're trying to
cheer me up, Okonogi,

00:14:35.550 --> 00:14:37.300
I'd think you'd have ulterior motives.

00:14:37.380 --> 00:14:40.550
Or that because of your baby face
you smoke to try to look older,

00:14:40.640 --> 00:14:44.060
but you're still failing.
It all just falls out of my mouth.

00:14:44.140 --> 00:14:45.680
Is that... so...

00:14:48.060 --> 00:14:50.850
As long as I have thoughts,
they get voiced.

00:14:51.810 --> 00:14:53.690
That's why I thought

00:14:54.320 --> 00:14:55.980
I should just keep my mouth shut.

00:14:58.450 --> 00:14:59.700
I see...

00:15:02.030 --> 00:15:04.450
Thanks to you, we're in another bind.

00:15:05.200 --> 00:15:09.120
Everything was fine and dandy
while OTF was quiet.

00:15:09.870 --> 00:15:12.580
Why are they always making waves?

00:15:12.670 --> 00:15:14.500
Those darn Dragon Pilots.

00:15:14.590 --> 00:15:15.420
Hey,

00:15:15.500 --> 00:15:18.510
the Air Transport Unit
will be there to back you up.

00:15:18.590 --> 00:15:21.220
If you've got something to say
about the OTF Aviation Unit,

00:15:21.300 --> 00:15:23.010
take it up with Commander Sosoda.

00:15:23.300 --> 00:15:27.100
Your OTF needs us to follow in the air!

00:15:27.180 --> 00:15:29.480
You're always like this...

00:15:32.350 --> 00:15:33.480
I'll kill ya...

00:15:34.270 --> 00:15:35.110
I'll kill ya...

00:15:47.330 --> 00:15:50.580
The vertical stabilizer
is a little too close...

00:15:50.830 --> 00:15:52.960
and I'm not satisfied
with the front wheel...

00:15:55.540 --> 00:15:59.210
I kind of understand
why you picked Amakasu.

00:15:59.920 --> 00:16:03.430
You should be flying freely in the sky,

00:16:03.640 --> 00:16:06.390
but you're locked up here like this.

00:16:06.470 --> 00:16:08.220
Despite that, you still endure it.

00:16:08.720 --> 00:16:10.730
You have such great power,

00:16:10.890 --> 00:16:13.980
yet you stifle yourself
so as not to hurt anyone.

00:16:14.650 --> 00:16:18.110
Somehow, that sounds just like
what Amakasu was talking about.

00:16:21.740 --> 00:16:24.030
Sorry for my nonsensical ramblings.

00:16:24.200 --> 00:16:26.320
I'll be back after making the adjustments.

00:16:38.800 --> 00:16:39.840
Um, excuse me.

00:16:42.470 --> 00:16:44.130
I want to ask you something.

00:16:45.090 --> 00:16:48.220
Why did you choose me?

00:16:49.220 --> 00:16:53.640
I don't feel confident
that I can understand how you feel,

00:16:54.390 --> 00:16:56.690
especially since I'm nothing special.

00:16:57.150 --> 00:17:01.780
Plus, I offend everyone around me
and spoil the mood...

00:17:02.190 --> 00:17:04.150
But despite that,

00:17:04.530 --> 00:17:07.660
you still wanted me, didn't you?

00:17:14.750 --> 00:17:15.870
<i>What is this feeling?</i>

00:17:16.210 --> 00:17:21.920
<i>I feel like the mood is actually good</i>
<i>with this strange creature.</i>

00:17:23.340 --> 00:17:24.590
<i>What tranquil eyes...</i>

00:17:25.550 --> 00:17:27.930
<i>Why does he have such kind eyes?</i>

00:17:30.220 --> 00:17:31.060
E...

00:17:32.600 --> 00:17:33.680
E.T....

00:18:00.840 --> 00:18:02.090
She... did it.

00:18:02.170 --> 00:18:04.170
Amakasu broke out!

00:18:04.300 --> 00:18:06.550
Hip hip, hooray!

00:18:06.880 --> 00:18:08.130
Hip hip, hoo--

00:18:12.930 --> 00:18:13.930
That is not good.

00:18:17.020 --> 00:18:18.190
OTF is airborne.

00:18:18.770 --> 00:18:20.310
Stop the OTF!

00:18:20.400 --> 00:18:21.860
<i>We have no radio correspondence.</i>

00:18:21.940 --> 00:18:24.650
<i>It will be unknown due to</i>
<i>the absence of a flight plan.</i>

00:18:24.730 --> 00:18:27.450
Then set up a mid-air SOC!

00:18:27.780 --> 00:18:30.410
Amakasu isn't wearing a suit.

00:18:30.490 --> 00:18:33.030
At this rate, her life will be at risk!

00:18:38.330 --> 00:18:41.380
My skin is starting to tingle.

00:18:41.960 --> 00:18:44.300
Am I going to die?

00:18:44.590 --> 00:18:47.420
To everyone I've hurt
because of my frankness,

00:18:47.760 --> 00:18:49.550
I'm truly, deeply sorry.

00:18:49.630 --> 00:18:53.810
To my mom and dad
who taught me everything, thank you.

00:18:53.890 --> 00:18:58.310
Please forgive me for wasting your money
to raise me and for dying before you.

00:18:58.690 --> 00:19:00.980
I love you, Goro.

00:19:01.060 --> 00:19:03.940
I wish I could see you just one last time.

00:19:04.020 --> 00:19:06.400
You always purred for me
when I petted you.

00:19:06.480 --> 00:19:08.490
Purr, purr, purr...

00:19:20.250 --> 00:19:23.840
By chance are you happy
when you fly in the air?

00:19:27.090 --> 00:19:29.880
MOM: YOU CAN QUIT ANYTIME,
BUT FOR NOW GIVE IT YOUR ALL!

00:19:32.510 --> 00:19:33.640
Flight Leader Kakiyasu!

00:19:34.100 --> 00:19:36.350
Hisone Amakasu has made contact!

00:19:37.600 --> 00:19:39.600
<i>Um, Flight Leader Kakiyasu,</i>

00:19:39.680 --> 00:19:42.150
<i>I'm sorry this has gotten out of hand.</i>

00:19:42.520 --> 00:19:44.610
I'm still holding onto my life,

00:19:44.690 --> 00:19:47.980
but I at this rate, I might lose it
before I can apologize.

00:19:48.230 --> 00:19:49.740
I don't care about an apology!

00:19:50.200 --> 00:19:51.740
Where are you flying now?!

00:19:51.910 --> 00:19:54.200
How did you get a cell signal
from inside the OTF?!

00:19:54.280 --> 00:19:56.530
I got it! It's the rear riser headpiece!

00:19:57.910 --> 00:19:59.700
I can't pinpoint their location,

00:19:59.790 --> 00:20:03.330
but I've confirmed a signal coming from
the OTC prototype 16 safety visor!

00:20:03.830 --> 00:20:08.920
Maybe we're receiving correspondence
because Amakasu has the headpiece!

00:20:11.050 --> 00:20:14.050
Have the instrumentation unit determine
the OTF's position now!

00:20:14.260 --> 00:20:16.850
As soon as we have it,
send fighter planes to escort them!

00:20:17.220 --> 00:20:19.020
-<i>Amakasu!</i>
-Yes!

00:20:19.520 --> 00:20:20.350
Are you ready?

00:20:20.600 --> 00:20:23.100
I need you to do exactly as I direct you.

00:20:23.390 --> 00:20:24.520
-You got that?
-<i>Yes!</i>

00:20:24.900 --> 00:20:26.650
<i>You've got the headpiece on, right?</i>

00:20:26.770 --> 00:20:28.650
<i>Press the button on the back of it.</i>

00:20:29.440 --> 00:20:30.900
Y-You mean this?

00:20:32.860 --> 00:20:35.740
-The OTF control program is activated.
-Next!

00:20:35.820 --> 00:20:40.120
<i>Touch the PT-V2 module displayed</i>
<i>on the visor to start it up!</i>

00:20:40.870 --> 00:20:41.750
Um...

00:21:25.790 --> 00:21:27.290
FOXTROT

00:21:36.800 --> 00:21:39.760
It has changed from
Hotel mode to Foxtrot mode.

00:21:39.890 --> 00:21:40.720
She did that?

00:22:00.740 --> 00:22:02.160
It's beautiful.

00:22:03.580 --> 00:22:04.700
<i>Third Class Amakasu.</i>

00:22:05.080 --> 00:22:06.830
<i>Do you remember the landing operation?</i>

00:22:07.000 --> 00:22:08.040
Y-Yes.

00:22:08.420 --> 00:22:11.960
I'm supposed to rhythmically push my toes
toward my stomach,

00:22:12.250 --> 00:22:13.170
and--

00:22:17.880 --> 00:22:21.680
-Cancel! Tell me how to cancel!
-<i>Third Class Amakasu?!</i>

00:22:25.980 --> 00:22:26.810
I...

00:22:26.980 --> 00:22:28.480
I'm terribly sorry!

00:22:28.980 --> 00:22:30.770
Sheesh. Going rogue like that!

00:22:30.860 --> 00:22:33.940
Well, on the bright side,
at least she had that.

00:22:37.110 --> 00:22:40.370
That's a non-smart, flip phone, isn't it?

00:22:40.570 --> 00:22:43.330
Y-Yes, it is. What about it?

00:22:43.530 --> 00:22:44.950
Well, about that...

00:22:45.410 --> 00:22:48.080
OTF eat rare metals for meals.

00:22:48.370 --> 00:22:50.290
R-Rare metals?

00:22:50.790 --> 00:22:54.340
Everyone has switched
to smartphones lately.

00:22:54.750 --> 00:22:57.970
But his favorite food
is the flip phones.

00:22:58.090 --> 00:23:01.470
So you're saying he chose her
because she had a dumb phone?!

00:23:01.550 --> 00:23:03.930
Well, I can't say for sure...

00:23:04.010 --> 00:23:05.520
-That's right!
-Well...

00:23:05.600 --> 00:23:06.810
I'm getting a flip phone!

00:23:06.890 --> 00:23:08.350
I have a feeling that's not all.

00:23:12.810 --> 00:23:14.570
Yeah. I quit on quitting.

00:23:15.230 --> 00:23:17.740
I decided to try a little longer.

00:23:18.280 --> 00:23:20.070
Sorry! I'll call you later!

00:23:22.450 --> 00:23:24.830
-Excuse me!
-Did you find what you were looking for?

00:23:27.160 --> 00:23:29.660
I can't really explain it,

00:23:29.870 --> 00:23:33.130
but somehow... I guess...

00:23:33.960 --> 00:23:35.290
I think if I stay here,

00:23:35.710 --> 00:23:37.710
I'll find what I'm looking for.

00:23:38.760 --> 00:23:39.590
Huh?

00:23:43.180 --> 00:23:44.180
Excuse me!

00:23:44.640 --> 00:23:47.640
I like the orange-flavored Joa!

00:23:49.180 --> 00:23:50.940
Oh, that's right.

00:23:51.310 --> 00:23:52.600
STRAWBERRY YAKULT JOA

00:23:57.150 --> 00:24:01.030
I might be onto something
about that systemic bullying...

00:24:03.280 --> 00:24:04.120
Oh.

00:24:05.200 --> 00:24:06.030
It's good.

00:24:06.370 --> 00:24:07.660
TO BE CONTINUED

00:24:09.410 --> 00:24:11.790
<i>I felt something akin to fate.</i>

00:24:11.870 --> 00:24:14.420
<i>I'm only interested in your body.</i>

00:24:14.500 --> 00:24:15.670
<i>-OTF.</i>
<i>-Bon.</i>

00:24:15.750 --> 00:24:17.090
<i>-Otofu.</i>
<i>-Tres bien.</i>

00:24:17.250 --> 00:24:18.300
<i>-Oh tofu.</i>
<i>-Bondaba.</i>

00:24:18.380 --> 00:24:19.590
<i>-Oh tofu!</i>
<i>-Now then,</i>

00:24:19.670 --> 00:24:20.920
<i>shall we take it off?</i>

00:24:21.010 --> 00:24:22.260
<i>Masotan!</i>
